11: /**
12:  * Feeds the {@link LightScene} into the {@link LightRegistry} each frame — the
13:  * BBS-free replacement for IRLite's {@code LightCollector} (which walked BBS
14:  * ModelBlock form trees + dashboard replays). Because every {@link PlacedLight}
15:  * already carries an absolute world transform, the whole render-path renderer
16:  * machinery IRLite needed for live-actor pose is unnecessary: we register every
17:  * light up front in world coordinates, exactly like IRLite's scanner path did.
18:  *
19:  * <p>Called at {@code renderWorld} HEAD by {@code GameRendererLightMixin}, before
20:  * the shadow bake and the SSBO flush.</p>
21:  */
22: public final class LightDriver
23: {
24:     /** Max NEW auto-light shadow first-bakes to introduce per active frame, so a
25:      *  freshly-lit area ramps its cube bakes over several frames instead of one
26:      *  spike (a per-light first bake bypasses the shadow bake budget by design —
27:      *  it can't show a blank map). Reset to 0 whenever the pipeline goes dormant
28:      *  (shaders off frees the depth textures), so each shaders-on re-ramps. */
29:     private static final int AUTO_SHADOW_RAMP_STEP = 2;
30:     private static int autoShadowRamp;
31: 
32:     private LightDriver()
33:     {}
34: 
35:     /** Pipeline went dormant (shaders off): the depth textures were freed, so the
36:      *  next shaders-on frame first-bakes from scratch — ramp the auto-shadows in
37:      *  over several frames again instead of baking all of them at once. */
38:     public static void resetAutoShadowRamp()
39:     {
40:         autoShadowRamp = 0;
41:     }
